      "id": "0zqzz19",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Types of Protected Areas in India"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "National Parks offer strict protection where human activities like grazing, forestry, and habitat manipulation are entirely prohibited.",
        "Wildlife Sanctuaries permit limited human activities such as timber harvesting and private land ownership, subject to government regulations.",
        "Project Tiger was launched in 1973 to ensure a viable population of Bengal tigers in their natural habitats across designated reserves.",
        "The Wildlife Protection Act of 1972 provides the foundational legal framework for establishing protected areas and conserving species in India."
      ],
      "id": "wmypcpd"
    },
