    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Jim Corbett National Park (Uttarakhand), established in 1936 as Hailey National Park, is the oldest national park in India.",
        "Hemis National Park in Ladakh is India's largest national park and is world-famous for the snow leopard.",
        "Kaziranga National Park in Assam holds the world's largest population of the great Indian one-horned rhinoceros.",
        "Grazing of livestock is strictly prohibited in National Parks but may be allowed under regulation in Wildlife Sanctuaries."
      ],
      "id": "ii9pjdx"
